---
description: Security and privacy boundaries for the card vault app
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secure Card Wallet Boundaries

- Treat this product as an offline-first card organizer, never a payments or card-processing app.
- Never store CVV/CVC, PINs, OTPs, magnetic stripe data, or full track data in any form.
- Prefer storing masked PAN for display and encrypted PAN for retrieval only when strictly needed.
- Do not log card numbers, expiry, holder names, OCR payloads, keys, secrets, tokens, or user images.
- Do not place sensitive card data in analytics, crash reports, ad requests, or debug traces.

# Security-First Build Rules

- Encrypt all sensitive card data at rest; keys must be protected by platform keystore/keychain.
- Keep sensitive values in memory for the shortest time possible, then clear/overwrite buffers when practical.
- Require app lock protections (PIN or biometric) before exposing unmasked card details.
- Redact card fields in screenshots, previews, recents view, and background snapshots.
- Assume device compromise is possible; minimize retained sensitive data and support safe export/backup behavior.

# Agent Refusal Behavior

- Refuse requests that add CVV storage, plaintext card storage, unsafe logging, or hardcoded crypto keys.
- Refuse features that send full card data to ad networks or unrelated third-party endpoints.
- If a requested change weakens security, propose a safer alternative and explain why.
